    {
      "id": "mferdqf",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "1. Background of Economic Reforms"
    },
    {
      "type": "keyFacts",
      "title": "Key Takeaways",
      "items": [
        "Economic Reforms were initiated in 1991 to address a severe Balance of Payments (BoP) crisis.",
        "Liberalization removed industrial licensing requirements, tariff barriers, and foreign trade restrictions.",
        "Privatization encouraged disinvestment in public sector undertakings (PSUs) and increased private participation.",
        "Globalization integrated the domestic Indian economy with the global market through foreign direct investment (FDI).",
        "The reform package transformed India into one of the fastest-growing major economies globally."
      ],
      "id": "83fq92e"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yrlwq42",
      "content": "• In 1991, India faced a severe economic crisis."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "44i2czl",
      "content": "• Foreign exchange reserves were very low."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "5frbb0n",
      "content": "• The government introduced economic reforms to stabilize the economy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x2lnarc",
      "content": "• The reforms aimed to promote liberalization, privatization and globalization."
    },
    {
      "id": "d7t30j4",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "2. Liberalization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "g9wne2s",
      "content": "• Liberalization refers to the removal of government restrictions on economic activities."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "newu7rc",
      "content": "• It encourages private sector participation."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "yu33yl0",
      "content": "• It reduces government control over industries."
    },
    {
      "id": "877xtdq",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "3. Privatization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "lzhzmdc",
      "content": "• Privatization means transferring ownership of public sector enterprises to private sector."
    },
    {
      "type": "pullQuote",
      "content": "Economic Reforms in India",
      "id": "ke6gsf7"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "k3zgaud",
      "content": "• It improves efficiency and productivity."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "z0pztdy",
      "content": "• It reduces the financial burden on the government."
    },
    {
      "id": "chk4yxg",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "4. Globalization"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "x7ogf3f",
      "content": "• Globalization refers to the integration of the Indian economy with the world economy."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "1qstcac",
      "content": "• It promotes international trade and investment."
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "id": "c7foa00",
      "content": "• It allows foreign companies to invest in India."
    },
    {
      "id": "ytjxhnc",
